From: CeRRiLLo89 <56557070+CeRRiLLo89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:55:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 223/226] CachedAppOptimizer: skip unsupported system memcg
 compaction

System compaction unconditionally applies the CompactFull process profile to non-application processes.

On devices without a valid memory.reclaim memcg profile this produces repeated failed cgroup operations. Reuse the existing cached profile validation before scheduling global system compaction.

Per-process compaction and the process_madvise fallback remain unchanged.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/am/CachedAppOptimizer.java    | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CachedAppOptimizer.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CachedAppOptimizer.java
index 75ca8260df..426f459a79 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CachedAppOptimizer.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/CachedAppOptimizer.java
@@ -1868,6 +1868,9 @@ public class CachedAppOptimizer {
                     break;
                 }
                 case COMPACT_SYSTEM_MSG: {
+                    if (!profileValidForMemcg(CompactProfile.FULL)) {
+                        break;
+                    }
                     Trace.traceBegin(Trace.TRACE_TAG_ACTIVITY_MANAGER, "compactSystem");
                     long memFreedBefore = getMemoryFreedCompaction();
                     compactSystem();
